# Review policy (process-options.md "Unattended operation" — the reviewer
# dial). One value on the last line — how many independent fresh-context
# review verdicts a completed work item gets before the integrator accepts it:
#   0 — no mechanized review leg (harness gates only; attended repos where the
#       human reads every diff anyway).
#   1 — one reviewer session (the default): fresh context, no shared
#       transcript with the implementer; input = the diff + the WI + the TCs;
#       output = a recorded verdict (review doc / docs/log.md).
#   2 — two reviewers with SPLIT charters, never duplicated coverage:
#       A = method / risk / corner cases (adversarial correctness),
#       B = process / trace / prose (SSOT, traceability, TC text, doc
#       honesty). Cross-provider is the recommended pairing (decorrelated
#       blind spots) — route via AGENT_CMD_MAP / the dispatcher convention.
# Floors above the dial: a gate advance under gate-policy `autonomous` always
# needs >=1 recorded verdict; a WI touching the spine registries recommends 2.
# The dial is read by the integrator and the run-phase convention
# (REVIEW-A / REVIEW-B sessions via AGENT_MODEL_MAP / AGENT_CMD_MAP keys);
# the coordinator loop surfaces it at run start but never enforces it — the
# harness pass is the entry ticket, the review is the judgment.
1
